    "body": "An initial Issue proposal could be re-read after owner progress and restart failed work through legacy scheduling semantics. The real loop now checks an optional owner-issued initial revision before promotion and commits first-admission identity in its existing effect ledger. Removing an order from active work cannot make it new initial work again; legacy explicit restart/amendment remains supported.\n\nValidation on head `75ae4f12808004cfc83d39b8306234e94d9e3ef3`: full `pnpm check` passed with clean source; exact-head Test run [35115224453](https://github.com/ed3c/noodle/actions/runs/35115224453) passed. A child process is killed after durable admission and before proposal deletion, then the owner reloads from disk and refuses replay. Six narrowly removed enforcement controls fail against the same frozen observer; corrected controls and legal legacy/independent work pass. [Immutable evidence](https://github.com/ed3c/noodle/tree/e7d37d4bf5dc6005f5d1eb5e342c4b97e4749442/evidence/82/initial-admission).\n\nThese are real local owner controls over temporary state; worker/provider adapters in them are test doubles. This supplies Noodle's ownership boundary for Soodles #18, whose real consumers, authorization, worker revalidation and delivery remain separate.\n\nRefs ed3c/noodle#82",
